  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive). Compound verb: {泣|な}く + {出|だ}す.\n\nNUANCE: The {出|だ}す component emphasizes the sudden onset of crying. It suggests that the crying begins abruptly, often triggered by something.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・{急|きゅう}に{泣|な}き{出|だ}す: to suddenly start crying\n・わあっと{泣|な}き{出|だ}す: to burst out crying loudly\n\nRELATED:\n・{笑|わら}い{出|だ}す: to start laughing\n・{怒|おこ}り{出|だ}す: to start getting angry",
